<VI _name="lvbd_layout_dump.vi" description="Reads the geometry of a VI's whole block diagram for lvai_layout_diagram, nested diagrams included, as one text line per diagram, object and wire. Read-only\3A the VI is opened by path, read and closed, never saved.\0A\0AA queue of diagrams is walked breadth first. Every diagram gets an id - 0 for the top level, then parent id.object index.frame index - so an object is addressed by its diagram id and its index in that diagram's All Objects[], which LabVIEW keeps in a stable order (measured 2026-10-16\3A NI's Clean Up Diagram moved every object of a DQMH Main.vi and changed no index).\0A\0ALINES\3A D|id|left|top|width|height for a diagram. O|id|index|class|left|top|width|height|frames|terminals|tunnels|own|frame|shiftregs|total for an object, where terminals is name^source^left^top^width^height~ per node terminal, tunnels is left^top^width^height~ per structure tunnel own is name^source for an object that is itself a terminal, and frame is width^height of a structure's Frame Size, which a write sets (Bounds is read-only on a structure, error 1029) and which differs from Bounds on a Case or Event Structure, shiftregs is left^top^width^height~ per shift register of a loop (Shift Registers[] answers the right one of each pair), and total is left^top^right^bottom of the Total Bounds Rect, which takes in the object's label. W|id|index|ends for a wire, ends being left^top~ per wire terminal. Every coordinate is LabVIEW's Position, in the block diagram pane's coordinates.">
